WEBVTT

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:18.450
We will now begin the trial of case
number 23 in courtroom 3.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:35.200
Your honor, the reason I have
requested this trial today

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:41.120
is to make apparent the stance of society
against these humanoid monsters.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.290
There is not only one humanoid monster.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:49.040
They are creatures that have hidden
deep in our society, eating us away.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.620
We must eliminate them completely.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:56.660
The case of the century, the judgment
of humanoid monsters, is about to begin.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:58.120
Many have crowded the building,

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:03.250
just to see a glimpse
of the humanoid monster.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:09.250
All the people of Libra City want
these days of unease to come to an end.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:09.250
I see. So that is your answer.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.080
This is what it is to be human.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.910
Intolerant and violent.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:17.370
You understand, don't you, Harazy?

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:21.660
We should go save him.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.330
Bem is in serious danger.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:26.000
Bem can handle himself.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.160
The danger I'm talking about
is that Vega woman.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.950
I can't leave Harazy alone, either...

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.120
I'm not going.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:38.950
The fact they're putting him on trial
means they're treating him like a human.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:43.450
Bem might actually be happy about
getting to be put on that joke of a trial.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.580
Do you really think so?!

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.870
You really love human-like things.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.660
You're the one acting like a human.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:57.160
You're just running away.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.950
Of course, I am.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.330
As long as I stay in this form,
no one will say anything.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.870
You both get disappointed because
you put your faith in humans.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.040
All you need to do is get along
with them half-heartedly!

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:14.120
What's wrong, Chris? Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:21.040
Yeah, got it. Then, I'll see you later.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.200
Considering the many lives that were lost,

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:35.660
Not even a lawyer.
--there are many who hope
for a proper sentence.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:35.660
Humanoid monsters aren't human, after all.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.120
It's our suspended Jeanne d'Arc...

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.250
I just couldn't stay still.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:31.660
Prosecutor, shouldn't you prove this man
to be a humanoid monster, first?

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.370
Of course.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:38.950
The defendant has been able to release
unnatural powers in his monstrous state.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:44.620
With that power, he should be able
to escape those handcuffs with ease.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.790
A normal man would die.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.870
How tasteless...

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.830
That was five times the electricity
used for the electric chair.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.830
A human would have died instantly.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:07.120
This proves that this man is,
without a doubt, a humanoid monster.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:12.910
Now, here is recorded
police footage of the suspect.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.750
Summers.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.120
It's for you.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:42.870
Nin! Nin! Nin! Nin! Nin! Nin!

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:45.500
Ja!

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:48.660
Nin!

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.580
Prosecutor, thank you
for this valuable footage.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.370
Defendant. State your name.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.410
Bem.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:04.910
The defendant has been charged
with the murder of Gavin Briggs,

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:09.160
as well as the murder of
Representative Harold Carver.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:15.290
He is also to blame for the increase
of various unnatural deaths in Outside.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:19.790
Now, there have been numerous
sightings of humanoid monsters.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:24.450
The defendant has been seen
working with two accomplices.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:28.450
These two creatures have
also taken the form of humans.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:32.330
The arrest of those humanoid
monsters are our utmost priority.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.290
Where are the other two?

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.200
Officer Summers?

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:48.080
The guys you call humanoid monsters
are completely harmless.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:51.040
He says they're good guys
'cause they bring him alcohol.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.950
Belo is a good person, too.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.040
Belo?

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.580
He's strong. At video games and in fights.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.700
He listens to our problems.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.410
Wait, who is Belo?

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:04.410
You all call him Gamma.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:08.250
Annie!

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.750
Everyone!

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:15.330
Actually, the police came
and asked us weird questions.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.830
Weird questions?

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.200
They said you were a
humanoid monster, Annie.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.660
No way. That's a lie.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:24.620
Of course. There's no way.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.790
But everyone is talking about it.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:31.040
Don't worry. We're your friends.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.580
Thank you.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.910
You shouldn't go to school right now.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:35.700
Let's go.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:36.700
Oh...

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:37.950
Huh?

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.950
N-No, it wasn't me!

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:47.410
Sorry, Annie!

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:49.370
Megan, it was you?!

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:50.790
That's because...

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.000
I told her to do it.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:59.750
No way! It would be so sad if we suddenly
shunned her away. We talked about this!

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:03.620
You said Annie was gross and scary, too!

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:08.750
Annie!

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.540
We don't plan on going back home.

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:14.580
Kevin's dad always makes up
a reason to beat him up.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.700
Maaya, too. Her drunk dad is really bad.

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:22.500
As for me, no one listens
to anything I say or cares.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.790
Belo is silent and doesn't
say anything unnecessary.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:28.540
But he always saves us.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:32.450
It's weird to hear everyone
call him a humanoid monster.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.910
Belo is Belo.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.660
Please save Belo and his friends!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.580
We want things to stay the way they are!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.250
You're not scared of them?

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.540
That's 'cause Belo is so kind!

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.290
Are you scared of them?

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:49.790
I will ask one more time.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:51.790
Where are the other two?

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:58.700
The defendant seems to be
exercising his right to keep silent.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.120
Your Honor.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:06.000
I would like to call a witness for the
suspected humanoid monster murders.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.750
Swear in the witness.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:20.000
I, Daryl Bryson, under the
just laws of Libra City,

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.870
swear my words are true.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:27.910
My father was murdered
by a humanoid monster.

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:30.120
Is that culprit here?

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.910
No, it was not this man.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.500
It was that young boy.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.120
Daryl, please continue your statement.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:40.700
Yes.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:44.200
My father was the secretary
of Representative Carver.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:49.620
Representative Carver was murdered,
just as my father was, who inherited his project.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:51.660
What project was that?

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:56.370
It is proof that Briggs was
connected to humanoid monsters.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.870
It is terrifying research data.

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:01.410
We are still examining the data,

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:06.450
but it is possible that humanoid monsters
are living soldiers created by Briggs.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:16.290
I did well, didn't I?

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:18.120
Yes, quite well.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:20.830
Hey, what will happen to Madame?

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:24.370
Did the people of the council
know she is also one of them?

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:27.700
This trial is that answer.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:30.080
Adults sure are scary.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:33.200
Then, we'll have to eliminate the other two.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.750
Especially Belo--he's a violent one.

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:39.450
I have obtained some
information in that regard.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:43.290
Everyone, I am Dr. Recycle.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:46.500
I have been researching humanoid monsters

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:50.200
and can be considered the
one and only expert in them, yes.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:52.000
According to my research,

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:57.580
humanoid monsters will turn
against us within 30 years.

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.950
This is a warning!

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:01.910
Humanoid monsters are dangerous entities!

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.910
They should be eliminated!

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:09.540
Hey, you!

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:10.830
You've been suspended!

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:12.500
Allow me to testify!

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.540
What are you saying after
causing all that trouble?!

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:18.540
Wait, Chief.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:21.120
Can't you let her go?

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:24.000
Even you?! What are you--

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.790
Hey! Wait, Summers! Wait!

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.790
What are you doing?

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:32.950
Our Jeanne is really stupid.

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:35.450
On top of that, she can't lie to herself.

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:38.200
She's nothing much. Just your normal

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:42.950
average idiot, burning with justice.

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:51.410
As such! We must tell the world
of the dangers of humanoid monsters...

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.200
The woman from the video stream.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:59.750
Oh, Officer Summers.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:02.250
Your honor, we would not have been able

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:06.370
to capture the humanoid monster
without her help!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.200
Please accept me as a witness.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.790
And, what will you testify on?

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.700
Everything I know.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.700
All right. I accept your testimony.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:19.540
Please step down.

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.450
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:24.040
Huh? We're already done?

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:29.290
Witness. Your statement.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.450
I must apologize to him.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:44.580
You were the one who
cooperated in his very capture.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.450
That was a mistake.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:50.700
The defendant was captured and
imprisoned at the fault of my own ego.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:54.370
Even though he had saved me
on countless occasions!

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:57.580
Saved you?

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:02.120
He has protected me from the true culprits
that were at the various scenes.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:07.620
Even so, I repaid his kindness with ingratitude.

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.870
I give my sincere apology to him.

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:13.160
You were just mistaken.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:15.040
You were also a target.

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:20.120
No, each case had a confirmed culprit.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:22.580
The people of Upper Town don't know

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:25.790
because they were not even informed
of the increase of unusual deaths.

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:26.870
Objection.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:29.540
That is mere speculation by the witness.

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:31.580
Accepted.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.290
Like the statement, "He saved me."

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:38.290
The witness will only testify
on objective truth.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:44.370
The charges against this
man are all a mistake.

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:46.580
I have seen it with my own eyes.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:50.120
The true culprits have all been
defeated by the defendant.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:53.620
Unfortunately, we have no records of that.

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.330
Without such records, there is no evidence

00:13:56.330 --> 00:14:00.290
to back such a statement, Officer.

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:08.620
I believed that humanoid monsters
were truly monsters.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:11.080
I even shot this man.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:14.370
However, after being saved multiple times,

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.830
I realized that he was not an enemy.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:21.620
Somehow, I used being "human" as a reason

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:25.200
to view them as a weakness of society.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:28.500
But that was all an excuse.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:31.040
I just wanted to protect myself.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:33.200
Isn't this city the same?

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.660
Objection.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:37.620
This has nothing to do
with the case in session.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.000
Accepted.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.500
Isn't it fine? Just let her speak.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:43.580
I want to hear her out until the end.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.750
People see things in different ways.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:48.120
That's right! That's right!

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:50.500
Silence! Silence in the court!

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:55.540
All right. Witness, continue.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:58.910
Thank you very much, Your Honor.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.500
Transferring to Outside,

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:06.200
I saw that this city was like our own heart.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.540
Separated into Upper Town and Outside,

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.870
an obvious division of the
rich and poor was created.

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:14.040
It was structured to build discrimination.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:19.620
We look at the weak and think that
we are safe and secure in comparison.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:23.290
Do you not believe that is how
we see humanoid monsters, as well?!

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:26.250
When we face them, we cannot help

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:29.660
but realize how ignoble we are in comparison.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:32.660
For selfish reasons, we can
lie without any hesitation.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.540
We turn our eyes away from the truth.

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:37.160
All of that, to protect ourselves.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:41.950
Gavin Briggs truly wanted
to save the people of this city.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:45.620
The humanoid monsters were the only
ones who took action in the same manner.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:53.080
You and your comrades care for humans
more than you care for yourselves,

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:55.660
hoping for the happiness of humans
with your overflowing ideals--

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:57.370
That's enough!

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:59.370
What are you talking about?!

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:00.830
How unsightly.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.870
If you want to confess your sins,
go to a church!

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:06.250
Witness, I will accept most of your testimony.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:09.250
However, your statement just now

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:12.290
was merely a criticism
of society and not a defense.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:14.450
I will not accept further statements.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.120
But, Your Honor,

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:18.620
this trial is wrong in itself!

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.950
There has not been a single
deliberation on any of the charges!

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:25.620
Are you insulting the court, Officer?

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:26.500
No...

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:27.660
Then, let me ask you this.

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:30.830
Could you kiss a monster like this?

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.580
I would like to ask all the people
gathered here today.

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:40.910
Could you accept a monster like this?

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.540
Take a shot of the court gallery!

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.910
Anyone can say idealistic things.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:50.660
However, as I said before,

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:55.950
this trial is to decide the stance of society
against these humanoid monsters.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:59.040
There is no need for any
other kind of deliberation!

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:03.580
Silence. Will the prosecutor
and witness both calm down.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:07.000
Your Honor, I requested this trial

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:11.080
to make known the dangers
of humanoid monsters.

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:16.000
We must quickly conclude
this trial and eliminate them!

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:21.410
The Libra City Council has also sent
a document voicing the same opinion.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:24.040
"Humanoid monsters should be executed."

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.370
No way! They are interfering with
the freedom of the judiciary branch!

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:29.700
Silence! Silence in the court!

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:33.330
The prosecutor agrees with the council.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.160
Humanoid monsters should be executed.

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:38.330
Your Honor, please give us your verdict.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:45.330
I will now announce the verdict.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:47.410
The defendant is sentenced to death.

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:52.750
Your Honor, humanoid monsters are evil.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:56.580
The execution should be done quickly,
as early as tomorrow morning.

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:58.200
Accepted.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:00.200
I believe a public execution
would be appropriate.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:01.500
Please wait!

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:05.660
They are not evil! They have been
protecting this city and all of us!

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:10.290
The verdict has already
been given, Officer Summers.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.500
Wait, Bem!

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:22.120
Let me go! I still have things to say.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:23.580
Please, wait!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.120
Bem!

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.000
Sonia Summers...

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.250
Thank you.

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:38.250
I am always disappointing you!

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:01.700
You know what I am, don't you?

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.410
Everyone is so mean.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.370
Chris and the others were your friends!

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:10.120
Nothing good will come of staying with me.

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:11.540
That's how it's always been.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.160
I'm fine!

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:16.000
I see. Even with this?

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:26.410
Why are you crying?

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:27.450
I don't know.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:31.250
I don't know, but it's just so moving!

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:34.750
To think you were so cool!

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:38.700
Everyone runs away when they see this...

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:41.750
Were you trying to get me to dislike you?

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:44.660
Sorry. I'm going to go.

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:57.870
Who the hell is Doctor Recycle?

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:03.910
Don't you wonder what research that guy
has been doing on humanoid monsters?

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:10.250
Excuse me. Do you have a way
of killing humanoid monsters?

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:11.660
Of course.

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:14.700
We will burn him to death with electricity
10 times more powerful than today.

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:19.000
They have the ability to regenerate.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:22.290
If a single part of them remains,
they will recover.

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:23.790
I did tests.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:26.250
I tried killing them in many ways.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:30.870
The only thing that had
effect was that bullet.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:37.160
Thanks to my creations, I was able
to obtain samples of their body fluids.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:40.080
I am sure you want to know the details.

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:42.410
A fearful man.

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:47.250
Who are you?! Don't shoot!

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.750
Stop!

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:00.660
Who did this?!

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.120
Where is Dave and the others?!

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.950
A kid named Daryl...

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:21.120
Someone... Please save him! Someone!

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:24.250
Um...

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:29.370
Please take care of him!

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:45.080
You think too highly of humans.

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:47.580
I do not think so.

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:50.000
Poor Bem.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:53.250
What did you ever see in humans?

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:56.830
At the very least, not what you did.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:01.910
Come, can you even smile like me?

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:05.200
You don't even know
how to smile. Pitiful Bem.

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:08.790
Go have fun with tomorrow's execution.

00:22:08.790 --> 00:22:11.000
You seem to be having much more fun.

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:15.870
Yes. I can't wait to see the faces
of the humans tomorrow.

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:19.000
Humanoid monsters don't die.
